KG42.register("rules-4a406b4e5f7bea3709083feb",{"id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R010","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R010","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Local clearing price","process_stage":"pricing","market_meaning":"Local allocation determines the price-setting last allocated bid, whose price becomes the uniform market clearing price for that time slot. Scope: BMG closed-order-book double-auction design with 15 min time slots. Condition: When the described double-auction mechanism is used. A clearing price is determined in every time slot; prices vary with demand, supply and socio-economic characteristics. Scope: BMG stated time-slot pricing design. Condition: When the described time-slot pricing design is used. Energy surplus should lower the microgrid energy price. Scope: General microgrid-market pricing recommendations in the C1–C7 framework. Condition: There is an energy surplus. A lack of local energy increases the market price. Scope: General microgrid-market pricing discussion in the C1–C7 framework. Condition: Local energy is lacking. The local energy price may exceed the external grid price. Scope: General microgrid-market pricing discussion in the C1–C7 framework. Condition: Socio-economic reasons, such as supporting local renewable energy, are considered. The electricity price was predetermined and fixed at the traditional price for renewable energy in Brooklyn. Scope: BMG reported three month trial with one consumer and one prosumer. Condition: During this trial, in which the market mechanism was not actively used. Each transaction may have an individual transaction price. Scope: BMG proposed further market-mechanism trials, before selection of the final mechanism. Condition: If the proposed pay-as-you bid order book is used.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function pricing.local under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["clearing.local","pricing.local"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R010-E001","source":"clearing.local","target":"pricing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R010-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e16"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"BMG closed-order-book double-auction design with 15 min time slots. | BMG proposed further market-mechanism trials, before selection of the final mechanism. | BMG reported three month trial with one consumer and one prosumer. | BMG stated time-slot pricing design. | General microgrid-market pricing discussion in the C1–C7 framework. | General microgrid-market pricing recommendations in the C1–C7 framework.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e13","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e31","v141-b-g03-e010","v141-b-g03-e016"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"x_clear_t","symbol":"p^{\\mathrm{clear}}_t","meaning":"Uniform market clearing price for time slot t; the source identifies this price with the last allocated bid price and says double-auction clearing occurs at uniform prices.","kind":"operational","domain":"Local time-slot price; the source does not state a numeric range in the supplied rule evidence.","unit":null,"indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g03-e009","v141-b-g03-e010"]},{"variable_id":"x_last_bid_t","symbol":"p^{\\mathrm{last}}_t","meaning":"Price of the last allocated bid in time slot t, i.e. the price-setting last allocated bid.","kind":"operational","domain":"Bid price in the local order book; the source does not state a numeric range in the supplied rule evidence.","unit":null,"indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e11"]},{"variable_id":"x_trial_price_t","symbol":"p^{\\mathrm{trial}}_t","meaning":"Electricity price applied during the reported three-month trial, which the source says was predetermined and fixed at the traditional price for renewable energy in Brooklyn.","kind":"operational","domain":"Trial-period electricity price; the numeric value and range are not stated.","unit":null,"indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-e016","v141-b-g02-e15"]}],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"theta_trial_fixed_price","symbol":"\\bar{p}_{\\mathrm{trial}}","meaning":"Predetermined fixed electricity price during the three-month trial, set at the traditional price for renewable energy in Brooklyn.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-e016","v141-b-g02-e15"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Local allocation determines the price-setting last allocated bid, whose price becomes the uniform market clearing price for that time slot. Scope: BMG closed-order-book double-auction design with 15 min time slots. Condition: When the described double-auction mechanism is used.","expression":"p^{\\mathrm{clear}}_t = p^{\\mathrm{last}}_t \\quad \\text{(for the time slot } t\\text{; the resulting uniform clearing price applies to transactions in that slot)}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":["x_clear_t","x_last_bid_t"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g03-e009"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"A clearing price is determined in every time slot; prices vary with demand, supply and socio-economic characteristics. Scope: BMG stated time-slot pricing design. Condition: When the described time-slot pricing design is used.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-e010","v141-b-g02-e14"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Energy surplus should lower the microgrid energy price. Scope: General microgrid-market pricing recommendations in the C1–C7 framework. Condition: There is an energy surplus.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e13"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C004","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"A lack of local energy increases the market price. Scope: General microgrid-market pricing discussion in the C1–C7 framework. Condition: Local energy is lacking.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e13"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C005","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The local energy price may exceed the external grid price. Scope: General microgrid-market pricing discussion in the C1–C7 framework. Condition: Socio-economic reasons, such as supporting local renewable energy, are considered.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e13"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C006","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The electricity price was predetermined and fixed at the traditional price for renewable energy in Brooklyn. Scope: BMG reported three month trial with one consumer and one prosumer. Condition: During this trial, in which the market mechanism was not actively used.","expression":"p^{\\mathrm{trial}}_t = \\bar{p}_{\\mathrm{trial}} \\quad \\text{(fixed during the reported three-month trial period)}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local"],"variable_refs":["x_trial_price_t"],"parameter_refs":["theta_trial_fixed_price"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-e016","v141-b-g02-e15"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R010-C007","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Each transaction may have an individual transaction price. Scope: BMG proposed further market-mechanism trials, before selection of the final mechanism. Condition: If the proposed pay-as-you bid order book is used.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e31","v141-b-g03-e024"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e04","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p07-c2r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.2 Market mechanism","anchor_text":"g pp y g ensured without the traditional grid. The BMG’s market mechanism is implemented on the Tran","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 6","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Any prosumer $P_g$ and consumer $C_a$ willing to trade electricity in the next time slot, can submit buy or sell orders via their EMTS (C6) to the market. Any order includes an order quantity and price. The market mechanism (C4) is a closed order book with a time discrete double auction in 15 min time slots. For now, consumers constantly bid their maximum price limit for their preferred energy sources (e.g. local renewable energy). Prosumers bid the minimum price limit that they request for selling their generation on the microgrid market."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e11","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p07-c2r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.2 Market mechanism","anchor_text":", stantly bid their maximum price limit for their preferred energy sources (e.g. local renewable ene","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Similar to a merit-order dispatch, the highest bidder is allocated first, then the lower bidders are allocated. The last allocated bid price represents the market clearing price for this time slot (C5). Consumers that do not undercut the clearing price will be supplied by additional energy sources (i.e. hyper-local energy or traditional “brown” energy) allocated over a similar bidding mechanism or predefined prices. This is well in line with the market mechanism presented by Ilic et al. [26]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e13","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.5 Pricing mechanism (C5)","anchor_text":"The pricing mechanism is implemented via the market mecha nism (C4) and aims at efﬁciently allocatin","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Price signals should be used to indicate energy scarcity or surplus [31]. Accordingly, a surplus of energy should lower the microgrid’s energy price while a lack of local energy increases the market price. Economically speaking, local markets are beneficial to their participants as long as the average energy price is lower than the external grid price. However, if socio-economic reasons (e.g. supporting local renewable energy) are considered, the local energy price may even surpass the grid price."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e16","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p09-c2r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.3 Evaluation and discussion","anchor_text":"y p Nevertheless, the implementation of the further market compo- nents, i.e. C4, C5, and C6, is onl","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"The double auction market mechanism (C4) is cleared at discrete time intervals at uniform clearing prices. This allocation and the pricing mechanism (C5) are already implemented. Hence, C4 and C5 are sufﬁciently addressed for operation."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e31","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p08-c1r4__v141-a-M01-matching","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.2 Market mechanism","anchor_text":"Fig. 5. High-level topo currently implemented market mechanism, the BMG will try out further market ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 5","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"In addition to the currently implemented market mechanism, the BMG will try out further market mechanisms, including a pay-as-you bid order book in which each transaction may have an individual transaction price. The market mechanisms will be analyzed and evaluated according to their allocation efﬁciency before determining the ﬁnal market mechanism."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-e010","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p09-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.3 Evaluation and discussion","anchor_text":"C1 U The BMG clearly aims at increasing the local security of energy supply and at strengthening the","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":"Table 1","image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"A clearing price will be determined in every time slot. Prices will vary according to demand and supply as well as socio-economic characteristics."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-e016","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p09-c2r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.3 Evaluation and discussion","anchor_text":"y p Nevertheless, the implementation of the further market compo- nents, i.e. C4, C5, and C6, is onl","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Still, the three month trial period did not actively use the market mechanism as only one consumer and one prosumer were trading and the electricity price was predetermined and fixed at the traditional price for renewable energy in Brooklyn. Thus, a very simple pricing mechanism, i.e. a fixed price, was implemented."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e14","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p09-c2r3__v141-a-M01-matching","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.3 Evaluation and discussion","anchor_text":"C1 U The BMG clearly aims at increasing the local security of energy supply and at strengthening the","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":"Table 1","image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"C4 (U) The initial mechanism is a double auction mechanism. C5 (U) A clearing price will be determined in every time slot. Prices will vary according to demand and supply as well as socio-economic characteristics. C6 (U) Residents set their price limits for local renewable energy and choose their generation mix."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e15","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p09-c2r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.3 Evaluation and discussion","anchor_text":"y p Nevertheless, the implementation of the further market compo- nents, i.e. C4, C5, and C6, is onl","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Still, the three month trial period did not actively use the market mechanism as only one consumer and one prosumer were trading and the electricity price was predetermined and ﬁxed at the traditional price for renewable energy in Brooklyn. Thus, a very simple pricing mechanism, i.e. a fixed price, was implemented. Hence, although the market and pricing mechanism are implemented and operational, they have not yet been tested in extended real-life trial runs. In conclusion, we judge C4 and C5 to be only partly addressed by the BMG."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-e009","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p09-c2r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.3 Evaluation and discussion","anchor_text":"y p Nevertheless, the implementation of the further market compo- nents, i.e. C4, C5, and C6, is onl","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"The double auction market mechanism (C4) is cleared at discrete time intervals at uniform clearing prices. This allocation and the pricing mechanism (C5) are already implemented."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-e024","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p08-c1r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.2 Market mechanism","anchor_text":"Fig. 5. High-level topo currently implemented market mechanism, the BMG will try out further market ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 5","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"currently implemented market mechanism, the BMG will try out further market mechanisms, including a pay-as-you bid order book in which each transaction may have an individual transaction price. The market mechanisms will be analyzed and evaluated according to their allocation efficiency before determining the final market mechanism."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-bidding","v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-matching","v141-a-M01-participation","v141-a-M01-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"pricing.local","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e11","quote":"Similar to a merit-order dispatch, the highest bidder is allocated first, then the lower bidders are allocated. The last allocated bid price represents the market clearing price for this time slot (C5)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e16","quote":"The double auction market mechanism (C4) is cleared at discrete time intervals at uniform clearing prices."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e04","quote":"The market mechanism (C4) is a closed order book with a time discrete double auction in 15 min time slots."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-e010","quote":"A clearing price will be determined in every time slot. Prices will vary according to demand and supply as well as socio-economic characteristics."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e13","quote":"a surplus of energy should lower the microgrid’s energy price"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e13","quote":"a lack of local energy increases the market price."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e13","quote":"However, if socio-economic reasons (e.g. supporting local renewable energy) are considered, the local energy price may even surpass the grid price."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-e016","quote":"Still, the three month trial period did not actively use the market mechanism as only one consumer and one prosumer were trading and the electricity price was predetermined and fixed at the traditional price for renewable energy in Brooklyn."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e31","quote":"the BMG will try out further market mechanisms, including a pay-as-you bid order book in which each transaction may have an individual transaction price."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"ee400f65aa87e2fb06c1b4ad7a3d9d3f46d904174717a5ac3454e695108d0739","applicability":"formalized","reason":"The source explicitly states that the last allocated bid price represents the market clearing price for a time slot and that the double auction is cleared at discrete intervals at uniform clearing prices; it also states a trial-period fixed price. These support two limited source-grounded equalities. The remaining constraints are qualitative or procedural statements about demand/supply/socio-economic variation, directional price effects, possible grid-price comparison, and a planned individual-price variant; the supplied rule and graph do not provide functional forms or variables for those dependencies, so they remain not formalized rather than invented.","bindings":[{"object_id":"x_clear_t","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R010-E001"],"rationale":"The clearing price is the price outcome in pricing.local; the frozen edge E001 carries the relation from local clearing to local pricing."},{"object_id":"x_last_bid_t","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R010-E001"],"rationale":"The last allocated bid price is determined in local clearing and then becomes the clearing price through the clearing-to-pricing edge E001."},{"object_id":"x_trial_price_t","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The trial fixed price is a pricing.local exception; the source says the market mechanism was not actively used, so no clearing edge is asserted for this trial fixed-price rule."},{"object_id":"theta_trial_fixed_price","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The fixed trial price is a constant input for pricing.local during the reported trial and is not generated through the clearing-to-pricing edge."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R010-C001","node_ids":["clearing.local","pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R010-E001"],"rationale":"The equality p_clear_t = p_last_t is exactly the clearing-to-pricing relation represented by edge E001: local allocation determines the last allocated bid price, which becomes the uniform clearing price."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R010-C006","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The trial fixed-price equality is attached to pricing.local only, because the source states the trial did not actively use the market mechanism."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
